<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:38:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>UK: Village votes to 'secede' in asylum center plan protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86e4f46ff7d0c36814d8ae5f1216f8ec5463619ff5c890bac9e7a7d9639a8459</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:37:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T17:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826--f45e2135fb80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Residents of Piddington, a tiny, remote village in Oxfordshire in England, have staged a "referendum" on leaving the UK. They are objecting to plans to open an asylum reception center at a disused military base nearby.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Canada and the EU build a deeper partnership?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4aa52900378a58302bdc1b15d4cf778c63fc28ff4d8fee09070a0aea56d35dbc</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:37:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-build-a-deeper-partnership/a-79295388--5b1c7df95a13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-build-a-deeper-partnership/a-79295388?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Carney is known for standing up to US President Donald Trump. Now he wants to forge a "unique alliance" with Europe. But what could such a partnership look like?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Shock in Kosovo as Hague convicts former President Thaci</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d1a53f4f64bc897608fb6068fef971aea09250beef76e07b980e5187f13864</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:37:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916--a5436d550055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction in The Hague of former President Hashim Thaci and three former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has caused consternation in Kosovo — both among political leaders and on the streets. DW reports from Pristina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British-American writer Bonnie Greer dies aged 77</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed561930f359e3393680b095c9b9310bfc1109c78d1b0515353051abe5ca056d</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:38:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174--ca7cae1c3055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chicago-born playwright Bonnie Greer, who became a familiar face in British political discourse later in life, has died. Her husband David Hutchins announced news of Greer's death.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How the Houthis are also putting Egypt under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce203b7e1b1aff8c371820aa9f455c246e81f5ae16faf8d467559a2288ca4bb9</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:38:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthis-are-also-putting-egypt-under-pressure/a-79291103--b1d138b096dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthis-are-also-putting-egypt-under-pressure/a-79291103?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthis, a Yemeni rebel group, are expanding their control of maritime corridors in the Red Sea area. Their target is their avowed enemy Saudi Arabia. But the military moves also endanger Egypt.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Activists sound alarm as regime seizes Baha'i assets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a845e355378a3dcedf7852df7991fa20d209031465ff2dc3a9e9fed8192d6a</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-activists-sound-alarm-as-regime-seizes-baha-i-assets/a-79291138--d67cdfeb619f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-activists-sound-alarm-as-regime-seizes-baha-i-assets/a-79291138?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rights groups warn Iran is increasingly confiscating assets from government critics and members of the country's Baha'i faith, but also actors, athletes and journalists living abroad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reaffirms support for Ukraine after drone strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72d1eec290e42776ee25302c60c2456e1cdc5b1bb0259d7e70cf82331b6d12df</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144--da0463d9d7dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Russia's recent drone attacks on targets close to the Ukraine-Poland border, Warsaw has doubled down on its support for Kyiv and pledged a "nonprovocative but serious response" to Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola epidemic may have gone undetected for months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18b11963eb9e26381d6b032cfacd7c9b305e55365abf5b4d4f66950bba0d8f0f</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803--d84e2884bf66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deadliest Ebola outbreak on record in the Democratic Republic of Congo may have begun months before it was first declared in May.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:303d5ac1c9b5175f77c6513bc683d1b8d52479ea33f6e2edcf53311c353e354f</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo ex-president Thaci sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:061098c4944d9d39934c12e7c9be9899e29e5c763748ab5969a850b4b714234a</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344--737389b3e2ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Hague tribunal ruled that Hashim Thaci, a former leader of the Kosovo Liberation Army (KLA), is responsible for war crimes carried out during the war of independence with Serbia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's rights groups, EU call out LGBTQ+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adfbb3509a139b92ea4702b3163be172b6be25afe9b5f883e9121c1d5846cd9b</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021--701b89ffacea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several raids and arrests of LGBTQ+ persons in Turkey have triggered sharp criticism from numerous Turkish organizations — and also from Brussels.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why do authoritarian regimes target the LGBTQ+ community?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e9f6956d10410519add8a17ff9026776ad9fa5ae693196f2a9da7ab49c4a74b</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831--8b4048f7a695.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A recent crackdown on the LGBTQ+ community in Turkey is symptomatic of a wider rights regression, according to experts. It's worse under authoritarian regimes, but why is it such a popular policy for these states?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia faces hard choices as Houthis gain in Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36ba454b634b3c573d3d9eb99b6be407df733f04962744a868cf759845ebef5f</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-faces-hard-choices-as-houthis-gain-in-yemen/a-79274826--836e117689a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-faces-hard-choices-as-houthis-gain-in-yemen/a-79274826?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia faces growing security and economic problems as it seeks to balance deterrence and diplomacy during its escalating conflict with the Iran-backed Houthis in neighboring Yemen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
